nflict.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-20T00:49:05Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#35479629055", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Alfonso Enríquez, also known as Alonso Enríquez was Lord of Medina de Rioseco and Admiral of Castile.", "newValue": "Alfonso Enríquez (1354–1429) was the first Admiral of Castile from the Trastámara dynasty, a pivotal figure in solidifying royal power and establishing one of Spain's most enduring noble lineages. As an illegitimate son of King Henry II of Castile, Alfonso's life spanned the tumultuous consolidation of the Trastámara monarchy, during which he leveraged his royal blood and military prowess to ascend to the highest echelons of Castilian society, becoming Lord of Medina de Rioseco and progenitor of the powerful Enríquez family.

His career was defined by significant naval and political contributions to the Castilian crown. Appointed Admiral of Castile in 1405 by his half-brother, King Henry III, Alfonso Enríquez played a crucial role in defending Castilian maritime interests, particularly against the Portuguese. He commanded fleets in various engagements, notably participating in the Castilian-Portuguese Wars and contributing to the defense of the Straits of Gibraltar against Moroccan incursions. Beyond naval command, he was a key advisor during the minority of John II, navigating complex court politics and regional rivalries, thereby securing his family's position as a major force in the kingdom.

